<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Helian Chang</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 434</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Helian Chang was the second emperor of the Xiongnu-led Helian Xia state in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, succeeding his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/helian-bobo">Helian Bobo</a> in 425. Northern Wei forces took the capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tongwan">Tongwan</a> in 427 and captured him in 428. He was treated as a guest at the Wei court but was killed in 434 after trying to escape.</p></div>
